VU1 worker costs with the launcher's settings (the launcher always records VU1 microcode while playing, GOW_VU1_CAPTURA):
- Capture on the native VU1 path (captureMicrocode): it went through compiledProgramFor on every micro-memory change
  (~650 a second in combat): a full decode of the 2,048 pairs (the exact engine redecodes lazily anyway), a byte-wise
  16 KB FNV hash and a file-system query (NtQueryFullAttributesFile alone was 9 % of the VU1 worker). Now a word-wise
  64-bit hash is looked up among the images already seen this run and the capture folder is listed once; only a new image
  gets its FNV file name and is written, so the files are the same as before (673 new files of a run checked: names =
  FNV of the contents).
- GS stage push: the packet is copied before taking the stage lock (the copy under it made the stage thread and the VU1
  worker wait on each other for every XGKICK).
Measured on the ship with the launcher's defaults (full screen 1920x1080, 16:9, FXAA, 2x dynamic, sound, capture; Xeon
E5-2666 v3, RX 580; with 01-08 and -Codegen locals): combat 44-52 fps (average 47.6) -> 53-60 (average 57.6). With it,
capture off or 4:3 change the combat average by about 1 fps.

